<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:07Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Revisiting the delicate art of French patisserie</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcd56ad5bd1d9013355f43d4865b0687002a303ce75c3874b626b0257a599bed</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:45:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261027-revisiting-the-delicate-art-of-french-patisserie--0adc80aacb3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261027-revisiting-the-delicate-art-of-french-patisserie" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Entre Nous, we meet Nour Kandler, a self-taught pastry chef whose approach to French patisserie is shaped by a deep appreciation for its traditions and the rich flavours of her Middle Eastern heritage. She shares her unique perspective on pastry, where classic French techniques intertwine with cultural influences to create a style that is both personal and distinctive.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: A referendum on 'Bibi' Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30e9a7d5b88033eb610518e06619983e2725a4a0a8d50eebd11de5d1c7c8ec99</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:52:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261027-israeli-election-a-referendum-on-bibi-netanyahu--42870793125e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261027-israeli-election-a-referendum-on-bibi-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, October 27: The Israeli, Palestinian and Lebanese papers break down what's at stake on election day for Israel and its neighbours. Also, the French government announces its first major concessions to protesting high school students, hoping to calm the movement. Finally, Harry Kane's Ballon d'Or means Lamine Yamal and Kylian Mbappé will have to wait their turn.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli PM casts his ballot as voters voice opposition to Netanyahu outside polling stations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dc973dea193ba233a8b8a675127fb150def6cb04223759f9b801101757d2fa7</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:42:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-pm-casts-his-ballot-as-voters-voice-opposition-to-netanyahu-outside-polling-stations--664441f7283c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-pm-casts-his-ballot-as-voters-voice-opposition-to-netanyahu-outside-polling-stations" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu cast his vote on Tuesday (October 27) in Israel’s general election. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>England's Kane wins Ballon d'Or, Putellas claims women's award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88c24cd91f16fdf265634f4c8ec41a29e02c3aebe9ba4098dfecaaba38430c2e</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:37:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/england-s-kane-wins-ballon-d-or-putellas-claims-women-s-award--16d645364e90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/england-s-kane-wins-ballon-d-or-putellas-claims-women-s-award" /><summary type="html">Harry Kane completed his long quest ⁠for football's highest individual ​honour on Monday (October 26), the Bayern Munich and England striker winning the Ballon d'Or after a record-breaking season that cemented his status as one of the game's greatest goalscorers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Localised Russia-Ukraine ceasefire starts Ukrainian town facing starvation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d5df769df94f8f9ecb2ce39cb80a37dc5b1e66b53fb81f8520e6ebc59b647e6</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:34:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-localised-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-starts-ukrainian-town-facing-starvation--26b8d037fc17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-localised-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-starts-ukrainian-town-facing-starvation" /><summary type="html">A localised ceasefire between Ukraine and Russia took effect early Tuesday (October 27) ahead of a humanitarian mission led by US first lady Melania Trump, as missile attacks resumed in Kyiv. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv, Emmanuelle Chaze, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Get the Flock out': Americans respond to AI cameras in bipartisan backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06efd9b70531e7b48054cf0ce589914803c9c60e00aad2caca01fa12b42b44ad</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:26:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-united-states-get-the-flock-out-americans-respond-to-ai-cameras-in-bipartisan-backlash-midt--835d29b1fccd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-united-states-get-the-flock-out-americans-respond-to-ai-cameras-in-bipartisan-backlash-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">AI-driven Flock cameras made by an Atlanta-based company are sprouting up across the US, sparking alarm and bipartisan, citizen-driven campaigns as the new technology emerges as a 2026 midterm campaign issue. While politicians hedge and local officials rush to sign contracts, community volunteers attempt to address an issue with major implications for future generations. But it might be too late.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ballon d’Or winner Harry Kane delivers emotional acceptance speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3dc52110932d4911086313786766e9d99280fc13261931b7d3ad1486ae86be26</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:20:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ballon-d-or-winner-harry-kane-delivers-emotional-acceptance-speech--113fa0f87132.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ballon-d-or-winner-harry-kane-delivers-emotional-acceptance-speech" /><summary type="html">Harry Kane became the first Englishman in 25 years to win the Ballon d’Or on Monday. Kane scored 73 goals for club and country last campaign and smashed scoring records at the World Cup, where he captained England to a third-place finish.</summary></entry><entry><title>American rapper Macklemore begins 'Free Palestine' tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ecf7108862b73537ab2281ee774178b76c86801f017724977ac19cc570d8f00</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:57:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-american-rapper-macklemore-begins-free-palestine-tour--6da444186197.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-american-rapper-macklemore-begins-free-palestine-tour" /><summary type="html">The American rapper Macklemore vows to speak out loudly against the war in Gaza. He started his "Free Palestine" tour in Ireland, one of Europe's most pro-Palestinian countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Trump escalates anti-Muslim attacks against Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a5ed1364fe2952a0a3c3ad193ab39cd613bbf76cc4f86f160439e3bc711514f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:56:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-us-midterms-trump-escalates-anti-muslim-attacks-against-democratic-senate-candidate-abdul-e--f4a83701aa1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-us-midterms-trump-escalates-anti-muslim-attacks-against-democratic-senate-candidate-abdul-el-sayed" /><summary type="html">As the US midterm elections approach, the Michigan Senate race is splitting communities. Trump is escalating anti-Muslim attacks against Abdul El-Sayed, the Michigan Democratic Senate candidate, who could become the first Muslim senator in US history.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sudan: One year after the fall of El-Fasher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd8fc444d1cd23350ec9ebe92c9cd80f01ce12b886f2b9133712a4d6cc801591</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:46:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-sudan-one-year-after-the-fall-of-el-fasher--874d8fa8f1e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-sudan-one-year-after-the-fall-of-el-fasher" /><summary type="html">It has been one year since the fall of El-Fasher in Sudan, a city in North Darfur, which was captured by the Rapid Support Forces. At least 6,000 civilians were killed by rebel troops as they entered this strategic city.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications after recent unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13edaa2ef64ed3470c354ac283dc23ea278fcbe60982b946d7f4770ee0c8d69f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:37:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-after-recent-unrest--7a8cca00906a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-after-recent-unrest" /><summary type="html">Tensions in South Africa over anti-migrant protests have left in limbo many who were counting on following the rules to sort out their paperwork and status in the country. Calls for a crackdown on foreigners, particularly undocumented migrants, have sometimes spiralled into murder. In response to the unrest, the government suspended the asylum application process.</summary></entry><entry><title>French government concessions to students 'tactically shrewd' but risk creating new set of problems</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:357c5802995191129875fd7e6855923e7106d4ab16aa3bfccb8d8318b8561edf</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:35:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-government-concessions-to-students-tactically-shrewd-but-risk-creating-new-set-of-problems--306b230dc2d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-government-concessions-to-students-tactically-shrewd-but-risk-creating-new-set-of-problems" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry welcomes Oliver Davis, Professor and Head of the Department of French at University College Cork. According to Professor Davis, the government's handling of the student protests reflects a combination of "tactical confusion" and an inadequate response to deeper structural problems. Davis cautions the concessions offered to secondary school students merely "scratch the surface." Meanwhile, France's widening protest movement has extended well beyond the classroom, drawing in the Yellow Vests, trade unions and people from across French society, amid mounting frustrations over public services and the rising cost of living.</summary></entry><entry><title>Algeria to deploy army units to Niger to protect economic interests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4f11501a87cbbbc863ebb81e9eba4d8f003c7785315b55674205d91de8a3066</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:28:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-algeria-deploys-army-units-to-niger-to-protect-economic-interests--dda1a7fe9e79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-algeria-deploys-army-units-to-niger-to-protect-economic-interests" /><summary type="html">Algeria will send army units to Niger to ​protect energy and economic interests, according to a statement from the presidency on Monday (October 26). Algeria's Parliament held an emergency vote on Sunday on what would be Algeria's first such foreign mission since 1973.</summary></entry><entry><title>French protests: Student union leaders vow to keep mobilising</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab024be687dcaf1ec5835dba5651f0baf8620836ad63fbdb3678c32bb3b9b142</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:18:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-french-protests-student-union-leaders-vow-to-keep-mobilising--5057a3ae5412.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-french-protests-student-union-leaders-vow-to-keep-mobilising" /><summary type="html">In France, after weeks of student unrest, the government announced new school measures. Student union leaders said it's a first step but vowed to keep mobilising as they expected further proposals.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iraqi court sentences six French nationals to life for IS group membership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fb529beeeee5c37433cd742776e7ed12add34921c55ce3167db325fd34ca5ac</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:16:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-iraqi-court-sentences-six-french-nationals-to-life-for-is-group-membership--3e5d4146faaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-iraqi-court-sentences-six-french-nationals-to-life-for-is-group-membership" /><summary type="html">Six French men were sentenced to life in prison by an Iraqi court on Tuesday for membership of the Islamic State (IS) group, according to a source. They are ​among ‌47 French IS group suspects transferred from ⁠detention facilities in Syria to Iraq last year under an arrangement coordinated by US forces and Iraqi authorities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: Fragile co-existence between residents in Jewish-Arab town of Lod</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e897d0b413f3aadbb76273f9972d8ee6d4ff8e5fa8d5db9ad23acffdc73dc0d3</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:14:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261027-israeli-election-fragile-co-existence-between-residents-in-jewish-arab-town-of-lod--de028a4ce766.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261027-israeli-election-fragile-co-existence-between-residents-in-jewish-arab-town-of-lod" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls this Tuesday, among those voting are 2 million Palestinian citizens of Israel, some of whom live in mixed Jewish-Arab towns. One of them, Lod, has long been seen as symbolic of this coexistence. However in 2021 the town was the scene of violent clashes, whose consequences are still being felt. FRANCE 24's Stéphane Amar, Sandra Lederer and Josh Vardey report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Chad hosts hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees as regional humanitarian crisis extends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec04bdff8561463e0c33f5442656e3e84c60d3d186d28608cee18f98653f4df8</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:13:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-chad-hosts-hundreds-of-thousands-of-sudanese-refugees-as-regional-humanitarian-crisis-exten--ea71b37e071c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-chad-hosts-hundreds-of-thousands-of-sudanese-refugees-as-regional-humanitarian-crisis-extends" /><summary type="html">Sudan’s war is spilling over into Chad. A drone strike killed at least four people last week in the border town of Bamina, and hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees have crossed over in search of safety. Many of those who survived the massacre in El Fasher are still deeply traumatised. FRANCE 24's correspondent Harold Girard has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Syria slams deadly Jordan strikes as ‘unacceptable’ breach of airspace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09a8710e2a3a88ced95dd03698596d47de8ddfc04a57251f0f025182bf3c1123</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:02:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-syria-slams-deadly-jordan-strikes-as-unacceptable-breach-of-airspace--2b9a8e2f5e25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-syria-slams-deadly-jordan-strikes-as-unacceptable-breach-of-airspace" /><summary type="html">Syria's foreign ministry on Tuesday condemned Jordanian strikes in southern Syria in retaliation for a deadly church attack in the kingdom last week that Amman linked to militants operating across the border. Syria said the strikes killed seven ⁠people, including three children and a woman. Jordan said it regretted the civilian casualties.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Jordan launches airstrikes in Syria after church attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de76f8fabf82a67737aacab652d26f0bed6a117ee71ee06be5ccecb858245146</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:59:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/jordan-launches-airstrikes-in-syria-after-church-attack--27982e6f3f71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/jordan-launches-airstrikes-in-syria-after-church-attack" /><summary type="html">Jordan carried out airstrikes Monday (October 27) evening against armed groups in Syria in retaliation for Friday’s attack on a Greek Orthodox Church in the southern Jordanian city of Karak that killed nine people, the Jordanian air force said in a statement. Syrian authorities said at least six people were killed.</summary></entry><entry><title>Palestinians in West Bank fear further escalation of violence if Netanyahu remains PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b69787c3020d5522f9f465f5f99bec0b056d659b13edc054085296962c31e9b</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:50:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/palestinians-in-west-bank-fear-further-escalation-of-violence-if-netanyahu-remains-pm--1f5e2d22638e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/palestinians-in-west-bank-fear-further-escalation-of-violence-if-netanyahu-remains-pm" /><summary type="html">Ramallah residents say they hope to see Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lose power in elections. "Netanyahu remaining in power means that there will be a clash, a build-up of tension and an explosion in the region", says one resident. Israel has committed the crime against humanity of "extermination" in the West Bank, while continuing to commit "genocide" against Palestinians in the Gaza Strip, United Nations-mandated investigators said Monday (October 27).</summary></entry><entry><title>Israelis vote in first national election since October 7 attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0479b88b823fbf21750186e1e2441df6ca0784512dfa61bc4545633cf4b8422a</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:41:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israelis-vote-in-first-national-election-since-october-7-attack--c484a521ac8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-vote-in-first-national-election-since-october-7-attack" /><summary type="html">Israelis are voting in a pivotal election Tuesday (October 27) as their country wrestles with unresolved wars, continues to reel from Hamas' 2023 attack and is deeply divided over the character of the state and the right person to lead it. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more from the ground. He spoke with voters.</summary></entry><entry><title>Anthropic files for mammoth IPO as revenues and losses mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:361c8cdc4ee4676ed866f9696e29bffca4d0b26e915a622966816fed955f95e7</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:20:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261027-anthropic-files-for-mammoth-ipo-as-revenues-and-losses-mount--280589ede6ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261027-anthropic-files-for-mammoth-ipo-as-revenues-and-losses-mount" /><summary type="html">US artificial intelligence giant Anthropic files public regulatory paperwork as it gets set to launch on the stock market. Also in this edition: France plans a special disaster fund for businesses hit by riots and looting, and Apple's new top-of-the-line folding iPhone screen shows some unwanted lines of its own.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Azerbaijan: Rare protests over hijab ban in schools</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1aab45204cd2ebf1a470ffc46d78fbd0936eb9d6cc017b4e78c7695545ef641</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:16:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools--72dbcc5dfced.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools" /><summary type="html">In Azerbaijan, a new government ban on hijab in schools has provoked rare public protests. The ban prohibits clothing deemed "incompatible with the secular principles of general education". While it does not mention Islamic hijab, girls and teachers wearing hijab have been turned away from schools. The measure has sparked tensions in a country where 96% of the population is Muslim.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu's political survival on the line as Israel heads to the polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eee12fc183939ec226fb69d64d7a3756957d6fc8de14bf22def41093bd3b60fd</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:14:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-s-political-survival-on-the-line-as-israel-heads-to-the-polls--b5fbf6bedec9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-s-political-survival-on-the-line-as-israel-heads-to-the-polls" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu faces a fight for political survival in Israel's election on Tuesday (October 27), with voters weighing his leadership after the 2023 Hamas-led attacks, wars in Gaza and with Iran, and Israel's deepening international isolation. FRANCE24's Douglas Herbert gives us his analysis.</summary></entry></feed>
